     230	Adding (5), (6), and (7) gives the full identity
     231	\[
     232	\boxed{
     233	\frac{d}{dt}\mathcal E_{BD}(t)
     234	=-\mathcal D_{BD}(t)
     235	+\int_{\partial\Omega}(u_t+a u)\lambda\cdot n\,ds,}
     236	\tag{8}
     237	\]
     238	where
     239	\[
     240	\boxed{
     241	\begin{aligned}
     242	\mathcal D_{BD}
     243	=\int_\Omega \{&
     244	|\lambda|^2_{\Gamma_1(I+a^{-1}\Gamma_1)}
     245	+\frac{b}{a}|\nabla u|^2+\mu e\,ab u^2\\
     246	&+\frac{\mu}{\chi}\left[
     247	\tau P_t^2+\tau(a^2-b)P^2+abq^2
     248	\right]\}\,dxdy .
     249	\end{aligned}}
     250	\tag{9}
     251	\]
     252	All displayed terms in \(\mathcal D_{BD}\) are nonnegative for
     253	\(\sigma_x,\sigma_y\ge0\), \(a>0\), and positive material parameters.  Under PEC
     254	or canceling transmission flux, (8) gives
     255	\[
     256	\mathcal E_{BD}(t)+\int_0^t\mathcal D_{BD}(r)\,dr\le \mathcal E_{BD}(0).
     257	\]
     258	
     259	## Classification and nullspace
     260	
     261	This is a full two-dimensional constant-coefficient dissipative identity for an
     262	exact stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML, written in Baffet-type
     263	time-integrated variables.  It is non-increasing, not strictly decreasing on the
     264	whole computational domain.  The nullspace contains the already identified
     265	undamped physical-region stationary magnetic modes; in the PML block, the
     266	dissipation also leaves the standard primitive-variable gauge modes unless fixed
     267	by boundary/transmission compatibility.  Thus the sharp statement is
     268	non-increase plus a characterized nullspace/no-abnormal-growth estimate, not
     269	strict decay of every nonzero whole-domain state.
     270	
     271	For spatially varying damping profiles, this artifact does not claim an energy
     272	identity.  As in the Baffet reference, the verified scope is constant
     273	coefficients, and piecewise constant layers are handled blockwise with
     274	transmission flux cancellation.

